<article class="env-lemma" id="0H74">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0H74">Lemma <span data-tag="0H74">15.13.3</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring and $S$ a smooth $R$-algebra. Assume that $A$ is an $R$-algebra and $(A,I)$ is a henselian pair. Then any $R$-algebra map $S \to A/I$ can be lifted to an $R$-algebra map $S \to A$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\tau : S \to A/I$ be an $R$-algebra map. Observe that $S \otimes _ R A$ is a smooth $A$-algebra by Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00T4" data-tag="00T4">10.137.3</a>. Thus by Lemma <a href="/tag/07M7" data-tag="07M7">15.9.14</a> we can lift the induced map $S \otimes _ R A \to A/I$ to an $A$-algebra homorphism $S \otimes _ R A \to A'$ where $A \to A'$ is étale and induces an isomorphism $A/I \to A'/IA'$. Since $(A, I)$ is henselian there is an $A$-algebra map $A' \to A$, see Lemma <a href="/tag/09XI" data-tag="09XI">15.11.6</a>. The composition $S \to S \otimes _ R A \to A' \to A$ is the desired lift. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>